#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:10028
#: 63223f0d6051438d91c4ed0197ab9138
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"In this notebook we guide you through what a typical MMM first iteration "
"looks like (note that what a first iteration means depends on the "
"business context). We focus on the application of the model for a "
"concrete business case. If you want to know more about the model "
"specification please refer to the {ref}`mmm_example` notebook."
msgstr ""
"En este cuaderno te guiamos a través de cómo se ve una primera iteración "
"típica de MMM (ten en cuenta que lo que significa una primera iteración "
"depende del contexto empresarial). Nos centramos en la aplicación del "
"modelo para un caso de negocio concreto. Si deseas saber más sobre la "
"especificación del modelo, por favor consulta el cuaderno "
"{ref}`mmm_example`."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:20002
#: 5f8629229aa941ad81968839845ac465
msgid "Prepare Notebook"
msgstr "Preparar Cuaderno"

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:20004
#: d254bd9244f5407ea622a5f141441a38
msgid "We load the necessary libraries and set the notebook's configuration."
msgstr "Cargamos las bibliotecas necesarias y configuramos el cuaderno."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:50002
#: de986b27158649fcb6e3ba955202f2bf
msgid "Load Data"
msgstr "Cargar Datos"

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:50004
#: 9e09434ec52a4c9fbe18869c2024d35f
msgid ""
"We load the data from a CSV file as a pandas DataFrame. We also do some "
"light data cleaning following the filtering of the original case study. "
"In essence, we are filtering and renaming certain marketing channels."
msgstr ""
"Cargamos los datos de un archivo CSV como un DataFrame de pandas. También"
" realizamos una limpieza ligera de datos siguiendo el filtrado del caso "
"de estudio original. En esencia, estamos filtrando y renombrando ciertos "
"canales de marketing."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:70002
#: 0f40259de62744a9a1455989298db1e6
msgid "Exploratory Data Analysis"
msgstr "Análisis Exploratorio de Datos"

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:70004
#: 33f474d32f9545159465a23b375d57ee
msgid ""
"We should always start looking at the data! We can start by plotting the "
"target variable, i.e. the sales."
msgstr ""
"¡Siempre deberíamos comenzar observando los datos! Podemos comenzar "
"graficando la variable objetivo, es decir, las ventas."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:70006
#: a272febf56ab4c83b3fc5fece5e92877
msgid ""
"**Business Context**: Understanding the sales patterns and trends is "
"crucial for setting realistic expectations for marketing impact. The "
"baseline sales level and seasonality patterns inform how much incremental"
" lift we can expect from marketing activities."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:90002
#: 254fa79f670848a39870e9eaf0a8bc2b
msgid ""
"This time series, which comes in weekly granularity, has a clear yearly "
"seasonality pattern and apparently a mild downward trend."
msgstr ""
"Esta serie temporal, que viene en granularidad semanal, tiene un claro "
"patrón de estacionalidad anual y aparentemente una ligera tendencia "
"descendente."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:100002
#: d3e024b94bf8460e98449ef87151c7bb
msgid ""
"Next, let's look into the marketing channels spend data. We first look "
"into the share to get a feeling on the relative spend across channels."
msgstr ""
"A continuación, analicemos los datos de gasto de los canales de "
"marketing. Primero miramos la participación para tener una idea del gasto"
" relativo entre canales."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:120002
#: 1535e2628a7448f294e98d53685a92ed
msgid ""
"In this specific example we see that `Direct Mail` is the channel with "
"the highest spend, followed by `Newspaper` and `Online Display`."
msgstr ""
"En este ejemplo específico vemos que `Direct Mail` es el canal con el "
"gasto más alto, seguido de `Newspaper` y `Online Display`."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:120004
#: 0e7f1ffa41bc4076b58ca82aa92f5e3b
msgid ""
"**Business Context**: Understanding the current budget allocation helps "
"identify potential optimization opportunities. Channels with high spend "
"but potentially low efficiency may be candidates for budget reallocation."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:120007
#: 13a8aa9cddbf4c509e261f83de98a499
msgid ""
"**Data Quality Consideration**: The spend distribution may reflect "
"historical budget decisions rather than optimal allocation. The MMM "
"analysis will help determine if this allocation aligns with channel "
"effectiveness."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:130002
#: d751904d2c2046f6b0adbf6238aa0f4c
msgid "Next, we look into the time series of each of the marketing channels."
msgstr ""
"A continuación, examinamos las series temporales de cada uno de los "
"canales de marketing."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:150002
#: 99472eb0763e4f018bbb49688f1f8b13
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We see an overall decrease in spend over time. This might explain the "
"downward trend in the sales time series."
msgstr ""
"Observamos una disminución general del gasto a lo largo del tiempo. Esto "
"podría explicar la tendencia descendente en la serie temporal de ventas."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:160002
#: bb142226f4b044cdb34c4f76bc0fe65f
msgid ""
"Next, we can compute the correlation between the marketing channels and "
"the sales."
msgstr ""
"Luego, podemos calcular la correlación entre los canales de marketing y "
"las ventas."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:160005
#: 10123bb7c8184470bb04effccb4f52d6
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We all know that correlation does not imply causation. However, it is a "
"good idea to look into the correlation between the marketing channels and"
" the target variable. This can help us spot issues in the data (very "
"common in real cases) and inspire some feature engineering."
msgstr ""
"Todos sabemos que la correlación no implica causalidad. Sin embargo, es "
"una buena idea observar la correlación entre los canales de marketing y "
"la variable objetivo. Esto puede ayudarnos a detectar problemas en los "
"datos (muy comunes en casos reales) e inspirar algo de ingeniería de "
"características."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:160007
#: 694288053293474bb06e0e4aeed09404
msgid ""
"**Business Context**: Understanding channel correlations helps identify "
"potential budget allocation issues. High correlations between channels "
"might indicate overlapping audiences or cannibalization effects, which "
"are critical considerations when making budget decisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:180002
#: 8854935e3da44ae5873aaf6c369f75e8
msgid ""
"The channels with the highest correlation with the sales are `TV`, "
"`Insert`, and `Online Display`. Observe that the biggest channel in "
"spend, `Direct Mail`, has the lowest correlation."
msgstr ""
"Los canales con la correlación más alta con las ventas son `TV`, "
"`Insert`, y `Online Display`. Observa que el canal más grande en gasto, "
"`Direct Mail`, tiene la correlación más baja."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:180005
#: bddcc5c665d141b991dcbeec513190af
msgid ""
"**Critical Assessment**: Low correlation doesn't necessarily mean low "
"effectiveness. `Direct Mail` may have longer-term or indirect effects not"
" captured by simple correlation. The MMM model will account for adstock "
"effects and saturation, providing a more nuanced view of channel "
"effectiveness than correlation alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:190002
#: c811c85896f74d04b469b1b1fc919236
msgid "Train Test Split"
msgstr "División Entrenamiento-Prueba"

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:190004
#: 2e88a6675b264cdb84be9a3c6b2d3d8e
msgid ""
"We are now ready to fit the model. We start by splitting the data into "
"training and testing."
msgstr ""
"Ahora estamos listos para ajustar el modelo. Comenzamos dividiendo los "
"datos en entrenamiento y prueba."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:190007
#: 71e6d7869dc04febbeaf5cc941febf05
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"In a real case scenario you should use more data for training than for "
"testing (see {ref}`mmm_time_slice_cross_validation`). In this case we are"
" using a small dataset for demonstrative purposes."
msgstr ""
"En un escenario de caso real, deberías usar más datos para entrenamiento "
"que para prueba (vea {ref}`mmm_time_slice_cross_validation`). En este "
"caso estamos usando un conjunto de datos pequeño para fines "
"demostrativos."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:220002
#: ac860552af70445a847b51d22a2d2473
msgid "Model Specification"
msgstr "Especificación del Modelo"

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:220004
#: 37c6c3d0c5a846a086e9d50cc990d972
msgid ""
"Assuming we are working on the first iteration, we typically would not "
"have lift tests data to calibrate the model. This is fine, we can start "
"with a spends priors to get started."
msgstr ""
"Suponiendo que estamos trabajando en la primera iteración, generalmente "
"no tendríamos datos de pruebas de elevación para calibrar el modelo. Esto"
" está bien, podemos comenzar con prior de gastos para empezar."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:220008
#: 5eb710dcdd704dd1b34bdd459d6c1093
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Ideally, in the next iteration we should have some of these lift tests to"
" calibrate the model. For more details see {ref}`mmm_lift_test` and the "
"{ref}`mmm_roas` case study notebook."
msgstr ""
"Idealmente, en la próxima iteración deberíamos tener algunas de estas "
"pruebas de elevación para calibrar el modelo. Para más detalles, consulte"
" el cuaderno de caso de estudio {ref}`mmm_lift_test` y {ref}`mmm_roas`."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:220011
#: df1a21ec07ef448b87cbed3b8c2c06f7
msgid ""
"The idea behind the spends priors is that we use the spend shares as a "
"proxy for the effect of the media channels on the sales. This is not "
"perfect but can be a good starting point. In essence, we are giving the "
"higher spend channels more flexibility to fit the data with a wider "
"prior. Let's see how this looks like. First, we compute the spend shares "
"(on the training data!)."
msgstr ""
"La idea detrás de los priors de gasto es que usamos las proporciones de "
"gasto como un proxy para el efecto de los canales de medios en las "
"ventas. Esto no es perfecto, pero puede ser un buen punto de partida. En "
"esencia, estamos dando a los canales de mayor gasto más flexibilidad para"
" ajustar los datos con un prior más amplio. Veamos cómo se ve esto. "
"Primero, calculamos las proporciones de gasto (¡en los datos de "
"entrenamiento!)."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:220014
#: 4193ecd8697c46a3b1d7f136a0e58a70
msgid "**Why HalfNormal with spend shares as sigma?**"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:220016
#: 3bc43a21463440d8a57fe69bae543483
msgid ""
"We use `HalfNormal(sigma=spend_shares)` for the `saturation_beta` "
"parameter (channel effectiveness) because:"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:220018
#: 238ff62283ae46859c824554c1f11963
msgid ""
"**Scale invariance**: The spend shares are proportions (summing to 1), "
"providing a natural scale relative to the data"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:220019
#: 0d31e662219f44cca715285ca1e8d1c2
msgid ""
"**Regularization**: Channels with lower historical spend get tighter "
"priors, reflecting our uncertainty about their true effectiveness given "
"limited data"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:220020
#: eca507bc8550493195af835dca78f8a5
msgid ""
"**Flexibility for high-spend channels**: Channels with more spend get "
"wider priors, allowing the data to inform their effectiveness more freely"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:220021
#: fe51365f3e974951bc97ced80f932f11
msgid ""
"**Non-negativity**: HalfNormal ensures positive values, which is "
"appropriate for effectiveness parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:220023
#: 847ee43d472849a7aa7fe489362a5d69
msgid ""
"This approach encodes a reasonable prior belief: \"We expect channel "
"effectiveness to roughly follow historical investment patterns, but allow"
" the data to update these beliefs.\" Alternative approaches include using"
" informative priors from industry benchmarks or lift test results."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:240002
#: 932a23bc0380445a8aade3f14403f3de
msgid ""
"Next, we use these spend shares to set the prior of the model using the "
"model configuration."
msgstr ""
"A continuación, utilizamos estas proporciones de gasto para establecer el"
" prior del modelo utilizando la configuración del modelo."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:260002
#: 8096d1a77f5a44dea7d8664254e87b9c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"We are now ready to specify the model (see {ref}`mmm_example` for more "
"details). As the yearly seasonal component is not that strong, we use few"
" Fourier terms."
msgstr ""
"Ahora estamos listos para especificar el modelo (consulte "
"{ref}`mmm_example` para obtener más detalles). Dado que el componente "
"estacional anual no es tan fuerte, usamos pocos términos de Fourier."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:280002
#: a63a50ddeefc4957a7bbdc01f0ed4f73
msgid "Prior Predictive Checks"
msgstr "Verificaciones Predictivas Previas"

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:280004
#: fe446d7dab6d43fda2102b6c2d594d1c
msgid ""
"We can now generate prior predictive samples to see how the model behaves"
" under the prior specification."
msgstr ""
"Ahora podemos generar muestras predictivas previas para ver cómo se "
"comporta el modelo bajo la especificación previa."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:300002
#: 4734cbe9627c49508681fe1a31694372
msgid ""
"Overall, the priors are not very informative and the ranges is "
"approximately one order of magnitude of the observed data. Note that the "
"choice of likelihood as a truncated normal is to avoid negative values "
"for the target variable."
msgstr ""
"En general, los priors no son muy informativos y los rangos están "
"aproximadamente a un orden de magnitud de los datos observados. Tenga en "
"cuenta que la elección de la verosimilitud como una normal truncada es "
"para evitar valores negativos para la variable objetivo."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:310002
#: 51f251168c3b4859a0bdb07b470801b6
msgid ""
"Let's look into the channel contribution share **before** fitting the "
"model."
msgstr ""
"Veamos la proporción de contribución del canal **antes** de ajustar el "
"modelo."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:330002
#: 03ed54591cbf4ec9b4c3496b500f9ee6
msgid ""
"We confirm these represent the spend shares as expected from the prior "
"specification."
msgstr ""
"Confirmamos que estos representan las proporciones de gasto como se "
"esperaba de la especificación previa."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:340002
#: d4ad089fc6544f25890e807c546c5557
msgid "Model Fitting"
msgstr "Ajuste del Modelo"

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:340004
#: 6e37150bb6374cb7bf7c7ee51e9c6581
msgid "We now fit the model to the training data."
msgstr "Ahora ajustamos el modelo a los datos de entrenamiento."

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:340007
#: 31f6723cfd4d41cca300229024a76bba
msgid ""
"**Model Assumptions**: The MMM assumes that channel effects are additive "
"and that saturation follows a logistic curve. In reality, channels may "
"interact (synergy or cannibalization), and saturation curves may vary by "
"channel characteristics. These assumptions should be validated through "
"out-of-sample performance and business validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../source/gallery/notebooks/mmm/mmm_case_study.ipynb:360002
#: 3e3521c08666424195ec27aeb5d849f2
msgid "Model Diagnostics"
msgstr "Diagnósticos del Modelo"

